  "title": "Two colonies that are strangers to each other",
  "question": "Is a fight between two colonies a thing worth watching here, or is it invisible at this size? If you cannot tell A from B, say so - that is the useful answer.",
  "context_md": "**Why colonies don't fight: one number.** `scent_spread` ships at 0, so every colony founds at the same point in scent space and every ant is every other ant's family. `nearest_foe` skips kin, so no ant in the bed you play has anything it is allowed to bite - whatever it can see and whatever its brain wants.\n\n**Both strips are the same bed, same seed, same 4,200 frames, same patch of ground.** The only difference is that number. Yellow is ANT 1, blue is ANT 2; they meet around the middle plant.\n\n- **A** - what ships. The two clicks are two names on the legend and one family in fact. **0 killings between them.**\n- **B** - the same bed with the colonies made strangers. **9 killings between them**, and no eye, no new brain wiring, and no species file was changed to get it.\n\nNothing is proposed for landing - this is the explore half of your ask, and if it is worth having it ships default-off with a dial rather than switched on under you.\n\n**The thing I most want to know is whether a killing leaves any mark you can see.** If B just looks like A with fewer ants at the end, then the fight is finished in the simulation and not on the screen, which by your own rule means it is not finished.",
